MCP, or [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/introduction), is an open protocol designed to standardize the way context is brought into LLM interactions. We’ll unpack this more later in the post, but jumping ahead - **yes, as the title of this post suggests - Sentry has an MCP server.** You can learn more about it by visiting the [MCP server address directly](https://mcp.sentry.dev), or in our [product docs](https://mcp.sentry.dev/).
The Sentry MCP has support for all the newest fun bells and whistles, including:
- **Remote hosted (preferred) or local STDIO mode** (we strongly recommend the hosted version. It’s lower friction and you’ll always have the latest functionality/stability)
- **OAuth support**to enable logging in via your existing Sentry organization, so you’ll have clear access to your organization and projects
- **[Streamable HTTP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-03-26/basic/transports#streamable-http) with graceful [fallback to SSE](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-03-26/basic/transports#backwards-compatibility)** if your client doesn’t support it
- **16 different tool calls**, including prompts, to support bringing wide context in from Sentry, including tools like project information, issues, finding or creating projects and DSNs, and even calling our [AI agent Seer](https://docs.sentry.io/product/ai-in-sentry/seer/) to generate root causes and fix issues (see the full list [here](https://mcp.sentry.dev))
The Sentry MCP can be added to most providers that support OAuth by adding the following content to your MCP Configuration file:
```
{
"mcpServers": {
"Sentry": {
"url": "https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp"
}
}
}
```
For clients that don’t support OAuth, you can continue to use the existing Remote MCP endpoint configuration. If your client doesn’t support Streamable HTTP yet, this will automatically fallback to the SSE connection.
```
{
"mcpServers": {
"sentry": {
"command": "npx",
"args": [
"-y",
"mcp-remote@latest",
"https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp"
]
}
}
}
```

